    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "Kinenth",
      "Cocktailo\nSherry Dubonnet Campari\nManhattan Gin Martini Vodka Martini Vermouth\nBloody Mary Screwdriver Whiskey Sour\nTom Collins Vodka Collins Daiquiri Scotch Bourbon\nCanadian Gin Vodka Rum Premium Beer\nMenus\nApériti\nCaviar\nFresh caviar with its traditional accompaniments\nSelected Gourmet Delicacies\nRoast au Vo\nA selected cut of aged beef, turkey or other succulent meat\nroasted on board and carved to order\nYour fight otten intri clise you of todays roast\nLamo Cury with Chutney\nF+\" 7152\nChicken Verdi\nTender chicken simmered with capers, olives and celery in a spritely sauce\nLobster Thermidor\nPlat du Jour\nRice Pilaf\n51z\nPotatoes Maison\nTossed Garden Salad\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nSelection of Cheeses\nFruit Basket\nCoffee\nTea\n*\nDessert\nDecaffeinated Coffee\n3-E\nSelected French Wines\nGreen Tea",
      "#* 0- 2A\nE-\nLamb Curry with Chutney\nChicken Verdi\nTender chicken simmered with capers, olives and celery in a spritely sauce\nLobster Thermidor\nPlat du Jour\nRice Pilaf\nPotatoes Maison\nTossed Garden Salad\nButtered Vegetable Bouquet\nSelection of Cheeses\nFruit Basket\nCoffee\nTea\n*\nDessert\nDecaffeinated Coffee\nGreen Tec\nSelected French Wines\nFrench Champagne Brut\nDrambuie Amaretto di SaronnoR Bénédictine\nCrème de Menthe Cognac VSOP\nCointreau\nJAPAN\nDong Kingman, the award winning Chinese-American artist, travels the world\nsketching and painting the beautiful, the monumental and the picturesque. His watercolors grace\nmore than forty permanent museum and private collections in the USA and abroad\n405.KJ003",
      "JAPAN\nJapan is a land of contrasts. It can display the most neon-lit,\nskyscrapered and expressway-lined face, yet find its inspiration in the\nquiet beauty of the graceful Tori Gate and Mt. Fuji, pictured here. The\nJapanese can run their trains at lightning speed, yet spend hours on\na small conversational courtesy. Here you will find graceful perfection\nand formality contrasted with vigorous commerce. Pan Am serves\nTokyo on its Round-the-World flights and nonstop daily from New York,\nSan Francisco, Los Angeles, Honolulu, and Hong Kong. Osaka is\nserved nonstop from Honolulu\nPAN AM\n2000.056.0572\nJ"
    ],
